#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# rotation_transform

#% text
# `rotation_transform(t), rotation_transform(t, p) (about a point of the plane), rotation_transform(t, w) and rotation_transform(t, w, p) (about an axis in space), rotation_transform(t, [u, v]) (in the plane of u and v)`: a transformation_function

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
r = rotation_transform(t)

#% cell
r([x, y])
#% output
#= [x*cos(t) - y*sin(t), x*sin(t) + y*cos(t)]

#% cell
rotation_transform(pi/2)([1, 0])
#% output
#= [0, 1]

#% cell
rotation_transform(t, [1, 0, 0], [px, py, pz])
#% output
#= transformation_function([[1, 0, 0, 0], [0, cos(t), -sin(t), py + pz*sin(t) - py*cos(t)], [0, sin(t), cos(t), pz - py*sin(t) - pz*cos(t)], [0, 0, 0, 1]])

